# Bench reads this file at startup. Copy it to .env and fill in what you use.
#
# Nothing here is required. Without an Anthropic key, specialists run on
# whatever `claude` login this machine already has; without an OpenRouter key,
# only Anthropic's models are offered.
#
# Bench looks in $BENCH_HOME/.env (default ~/.bench/.env), then the directory
# it was started from, then where it is installed — first hit wins. A variable
# exported in the shell beats all of them. Settings in the cockpit beats
# everything, for as long as that daemon runs.
#
# Only the keys below are read. Anything else in your .env is left alone and
# is never handed to a specialist.

# Bills the API. Overrides this machine's claude.ai login for every specialist
# started after it — including turning off claude.ai connectors, so leave it
# out if the login is what you want spent.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-...

# From `claude setup-token`. Bills the subscription it was minted from rather
# than the API. Use this one or the key above, not both.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...

# For specialists you run on anything other than Claude. Billed to OpenRouter.
# OPEN_ROUTER_KEY and OPENROUTER_KEY are read too, if that is how you spell it.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
